OA and OB are y=\frac{3}{4}x and y=\frac{1}{4}x, respectively.
Therefore, the triangle may be expressed as a vertically simple region by the following inequalities:
0\le x\le 4,\quad \frac{x}{4}\le y\le \frac{3x}{4}
The double integral of f( x,y )=-22 y{e}^{x} over the triangle is the following iterated integral:
\begin{array}{rcl}
\int_0^4 \int_{x/4}^{3x/4} -22 y e^x \,dy \,dx \amp =\amp \int_0^4 \frac{-22}{2} y^2 e^x\bigg|_{y=x/4}^{3x/4} \,dx\\ \amp =\amp \int_0^4 -11 e^x\left(\frac{9 x^2}{16}-\frac{x^2}{16}\right)\,dx\\ \amp =\amp \int_0^4 \frac{-11}{2} x^2 e^x \,dx \end{array} We use the integration formula \int {x}^2{e}^{x} \,dx={x}^2{e}^{x}-2x{e}^{x}+2{e}^{x}+C This gives
\begin{array}{rcl} \int_0^4 \int_{{x}/{4}}^{3x/4} -22 y e^x \,dy \,dx \amp =\amp \frac{-11}{2}\int_0^4 x^2 e^x\,dx\\ \amp =\amp -5.5 x^2 e^x + 11 x e^x - 11 e^x \bigg|_0^4\\ \amp =\amp
-5.5\cdot 16 e^4 + 11\cdot 4 e^4 - 11 e^4 + 11\\ \amp =\amp -55 e^4 + 11 \approx -2991.9 \end{array}
